# Unify demo UI components

Demo HTML that is the same widget must be **one component**, imported.
Do not paste the same JSX into a second `*DemoHelper`.

Demos may cross-import (see `src/README.md`). Upper-layer demos reuse
lower-layer chrome: `formChrome = { ...sectionChrome, renderHeader, renderForm }`.

```tsx
// ❌ BAD — identical appendix in two helpers
// sectionResponderDemoHelper.tsx
renderAppendix: (comment) => <div style={yellow}>{comment}</div>
// formResponderDemoHelper.tsx
renderAppendix: (comment) => <div style={yellow}>{comment}</div>

// ✅ GOOD — one chrome bag; the form shell adds only form-level slots
export const formChrome = {
  ...sectionChrome,
  renderHeader,
  renderForm,
};
```

Same for lock icons, remark cards, `useFieldMethods`. Shared **UI**
(`DemoPage`, `SidebarLayout`, `ConfirmBanner`, `DropdownMenu`,
`PhaseTabs`, `PhaseJsonPanels`, `EditorDialog`, `TextField`,
`FieldViewerChrome`, `RequiredMark`, `SelectColumns`, `FormTitle`,
`ReviewStatusNote`, `Stack`, `Row`, `SectionFrame`, `FieldRow`, …)
lives in `src/demo-utils/` — see `demos-are-wiring.mdc`. Package
demos **wire** those widgets; they do not own `style={{…}}`, leftover
`<strong>`/`<button>`, layout knobs (`gap={8}`, `align`,
`fontSize`), or chrome copy as `children` (`"Show deleted"`). A
control is named for what it is (`ShowDeleted`, `ReviewPending`) and
bakes its label. Named widgets take data/callbacks only.
If blurbs or fixtures differ, pass them as **required** props — do not
duplicate the widget.

`PhaseJsonPanels` owns JSON dumps. Do not paste a second `<pre>`.
`SelectColumns` is one column picker (`options` and `legend` required).
Fill and review field viewers compose `FieldViewerChrome`.
`ReviewStatusNote` is one italic legend. `FormTitle` is the form header.

`DropdownMenu` owns the popover panel (absolute, white, bordered). Hosts
pass `trigger`, `align`, and item nodes. Do not inline a second menu
surface in a package demo.

Review follow-up is a nested Design list under the origin item —
`FormDialogsEditor` (`sidebar={null}`) plus `followUpDraftsList`. Same
`AddFormItem`, `FormItemEditor`, Edit, and move as Design. Do not invent a
label-only draft list or a second item editor.

Empty follow-up (no items yet) uses a **top icon** trigger for `AddFormItem`
(same Field / Heading / Panel catalog). `+ Add item` is the list slot, shown
only after the block has its first item.

The required star is field-viewer chrome (`RequiredMark` in `src/demo-utils/`),
not draft/list HTML. If several field viewers show it, they compose the same
mark.

Design list viewers (field + star, heading, panel) are **one bag** —
`listViewers` in `form-item-editor/demo`. Do not paste `FieldLabel` /
`HeadingLabel` / `PanelLabel` into a second helper. Fill/review viewers
are **one bag** each (`fillViewers` / `reviewViewers`); they compose
`FillFieldViewer` / `ReviewFieldViewer` plus nested heading/panel.

Related: `no-html-outside-demo.mdc` (no HTML in library),
`no-optional-defaults.mdc` (library still does not invent copy;
demo-utils named controls bake theirs),
`demos-are-wiring.mdc` (UI widgets live in `src/demo-utils/`).
